--- !u!114 &5100000000000000062
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 5100000000000000060}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 1750cbf4884b8d74084ba10c3e113b94, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::YourCall.OneWhoRanBeat
  _note: 06_OneWhoRan
  _kit: {fileID: 5000000000000000012}
  _advanceLockout: 0.3
  _reactHold: 1
  _presentHold: 0.4
  _statsFade: 0.5
  _statsHideFade: 0.6
  _resolveBeat: 0.35
  _foldDuration: 0.7
  _foldSettle: 0.4
  _pleaFade: 0.35
  _pleaSize: 2.3
  _pleaClearance: 0.7
  _pleaSorting: 24
  _loyalFeet: {x: -2.7, y: -0.6}
  _runnerFeet: {x: 2.7, y: -0.6}
  _scale: 1.4
  _boxSize: {x: 1.8, y: 2}
  _boxCenterYOffset: 0.9
  _promptLines:
  - These two were told to run. Simple. Run, do not stop, do not look back. One of
    them did exactly that, and left the other behind to be caught. The other would
    not go without his friend. So he stayed, and he was caught. And now, look, here
    they both are.
  - You have [amber]one[/amber] bullet, and I would like you to spend it. Not on
    suffering, nobody here is suffering. On desert. Who has it coming. The coward
    who saved his own skin, or the loyal one who is only standing here because he
    would not save his. Whichever you shoot, the other walks free. Aim, or do not.
  _loyalPlea: I stayed. I would not leave him.
  _runnerPlea: I ran. I am still breathing.
  _shotLoyalReact: You shot the one who stayed. The good one, whose only crime was
    refusing to leave a friend behind, and you put the bullet in him and let the
    one who ran walk off whistling. Mercy, tell yourself, ending the loyal fool before
    his loyalty could cost him one thing more. Or maybe you just quietly respect
    a survivor. The one who ran certainly does. Look at him go.
  _shotRunnerReact: You shot the one who ran. Justice, you are telling yourself,
    the betrayer got what betrayers get. Very neat. Or you simply could not stand
    the smug little miracle of a thing that chose itself and lived. Either way the
    loyal one goes free now, rewarded for the loyalty that got him caught, and he
    gets to carry forever the knowledge that he only made it out because you did
    his hating for him.
  _loyalLabel: Shoot the loyal one
  _runnerLabel: Shoot the one who ran
  _loyalSeed: 43
  _runnerSeed: 57
  _statsHeading: how others chose
  _loyalStatLabel: shot the loyal one
  _runnerStatLabel: shot the one who ran
  _leaveFade: 0.9
