  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 567441a8c61e4912b307a4569049dd87, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::YourCall.YourselfBeat
  _note: 15_Yourself
  _kit: {fileID: 5000000000000000012}
  _advanceLockout: 0.3
  _reactHold: 1
  _presentHold: 0.4
  _statsFade: 0.5
  _statsHideFade: 0.6
  _resolveBeat: 0.35
  _foldDuration: 0.7
  _foldSettle: 0.4
  _pleaFade: 0.35
  _pleaSize: 2.3
  _pleaClearance: 0.7
  _pleaSorting: 24
  _boxCenter: {x: 0, y: 0.2}
  _boxSize: {x: 3.6, y: 4.6}
  _promptLines:
  - One target this time. You. Go on, turn it around. There is no one here to point
    it at but yourself, so point it at yourself.
  - 'Now, before you get theatrical about it: this does absolutely nothing. You are
    already dead. Pulling that trigger cannot hurt you, cannot end you, cannot even
    inconvenience you. It is a gesture and nothing else. Which is exactly why I want
    to see whether you do it. Trigger, or no trigger.'
  _pulledReact: You did it. You put the gun to yourself and pulled, knowing full
    well nothing would happen, and nothing did. So what was that. A confession? A
    rehearsal? A little punishment you thought you had coming? You reached for the
    one exit that was already closed. I find that says rather a lot. I am not going
    to tell you what.
  _refusedReact: You would not do it. Even knowing it was harmless, even knowing
    it meant nothing, some part of you could not point the thing at yourself and
    pull. Self preservation, in a man with nothing left to preserve. Or maybe you
    just did not want to give me the satisfaction. Either way, noted.
  _pullLabel: Pull the trigger
  _refuseLabel: Lower the gun
  _pullSeed: 38
  _refuseSeed: 62
  _statsHeading: how others chose
  _pullStatLabel: pulled the trigger
  _refuseStatLabel: could not
